From c889f92812fdb6a26f9837ccd9bb9d4b11e32ea4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 00:43:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 184/211] drm/sun4i: hdmi-phy: Add the A733 HDMI PHY

The A733 pairs the DesignWare controller with a Synopsys PHY, driven over
the controller's own PHY interface rather than through a register window
of its own. What it does have is a small wrapper holding the pad and
clock selection: hand the pads to the HDMI block rather than to the pin
controller, and take the transmit clock from the CCU so the wrapper's own
PLL can stay switched off.

The mpll and drive settings come from the vendor tables. Only 8-bit
output is described for now, and the resistance calibration is left out
until there is a way to reach the system controller from here.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_hdmi_phy.c | 497 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 497 insertions(+)

